1035 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 129 0 R
/T (Files left open after an error \(measured, error in the second of two opens\): with statement: 0; try/finally written correctly \(nested so each file is closed\): 0; manual code without finally: 1 file stays open \(the first\). With k files opened one after another and the failure on the last, naive manual code leaks up to k-1 files; the with statement and correct try/finally leak none. The manual version is also easy to get wrong, which is why with is preferred.)
/E (Files left open after an error \(measured, error in the second of two opens\): with statement: 0; try/finally written correctly \(nested so each file is closed\): 0; manual code without finally: 1 file stays open \(the first\). With k files opened one after another and the failure on the last, naive manual code leaks up to k-1 files; the with statement and correct try/finally leak none. The manual version is also easy to get wrong, which is why with is preferred.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [30]
>>
