/Title (import cost: the first import attendance.stats finds, compiles \(or loads cached bytecode\), and executes the module once: measured 0.755 ms and 13.1 KiB of allocated memory for the three sub-modules. Afterwards the module object is stored in sys.modules, so repeating the import is a dictionary lookup: 0.133 microseconds each. So import cost is a one-time O\(size of the code\) and O\(1\) afterwards, and the memory is small and constant \(each module is held once, however many files import it\).)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2400 0 R
/Prev 2415 0 R
/Next 2416 0 R
>>
endobj
