<<
/Title (Import forms \(demonstrated in the output below\): import attendance.stats loads the module and binds only the name attendance, so you must write attendance.stats.percentage\(...\); from attendance import stats binds the name stats to the sub-module, so you write stats.percentage\(...\); from attendance.stats import percentage binds the function itself, so you write percentage\(...\). All three give the same function object \(output: True\). The first keeps the origin visible, the last is shortest but can hide where a name came from or collide with a local name.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2432 0 R
/Prev 2521 0 R
/Next 2459 0 R
