2650 0 obj
<<
/Title (Measured \(200,000 lines\): LBYL stays flat at about 0.016 s \(about 0.08 microseconds per line\) at any bad-line rate. EAFP costs 0.0247 s with 0.1% bad lines and rises to 0.0260 s \(1%\), 0.0319 s \(10%\) and 0.0586 s \(50%\). From 0.1% to 50% bad lines the extra 0.034 s over about 100,000 bad lines means roughly 0.3 microseconds per raised and caught exception. Part of EAFP's base cost is the extra function call to parse_line, not the try itself.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2628 0 R
/Prev 2641 0 R
/Next 2642 0 R
>>
endobj
